error[ffi_layer_undeclared]: `hero_time_monotonic_ns` is the platform layer's, declared by its `hero_time.h`, and this group's header puts a call to it in the program's own code through a header that includes none of the layer's, so no group of this program says `layer` and its link carries none of the layer: name `hero_time.h` in this group, or include it in the group's header, and say `layer` after the header
  at tests/golden/unsupported/layer-a-name-a-later-groups-macro-reaches-is-told-at-that-group.case/main.hero:11:8
     |
  11 | extern "now.h"  #~ ffi_layer_undeclared
     |        ^^^^^^^
  note: the platform layer's members are compiled and linked only for a program whose groups say `layer`; a program none of whose groups says it links nothing of the layer, so its build asks nothing of it
  note: clang checks a binding against the header its group names, so a function of the layer's declared by the program itself is checked against nothing the layer wrote: a parameter or a result of another width there is a call the layer reads otherwise
  fix (guess): name the layer's header and say `layer`
